04:54.695 --> 04:55.897
[SPEAKER_00]: Like right behind him?

04:57.999 --> 04:59.480
[SPEAKER_01]: Five to ten feet distance.

05:00.263 --> 05:08.006
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, do you want to be like, man, so the thing is, you can be five feet behind him, but what I'm trying to ask is, do you want to be second in the line?

05:08.546 --> 05:09.127
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you want to be...

05:09.147 --> 05:10.287
[SPEAKER_00]: I want to be off to the side.

05:10.347 --> 05:11.688
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't want to go in first.

05:11.928 --> 05:17.790
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, the Warren, I know, but the thing is, is the Warrens, the passages are like that.

05:18.010 --> 05:18.390
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

05:18.910 --> 05:25.053
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he basically draws his sword, and I'm asking, do you want to be behind him or guide him to where you want to go?

05:25.073 --> 05:25.633
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, yes.

05:25.993 --> 05:27.454
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, so you start going in.

05:29.567 --> 05:33.973
[SPEAKER_00]: And you kind of realize why it's scary.

05:34.954 --> 05:39.640
[SPEAKER_00]: When you were on the tops of the buildings, you could see what was below.

05:40.300 --> 05:47.369
[SPEAKER_00]: But as you walk through the Warrens in the way that they are, you definitely feel like you're enclosed and they're blinded.

05:50.942 --> 05:55.247
[SPEAKER_00]: So you walk forward and you know you have to make it 100 feet to the building.

05:55.968 --> 06:06.059
